## 2. Complete feature blueprint

The platform can contain 15 modules, but they should share a common incident, location, notification and task system.

| #  | Module                 | Main capabilities                                                             | Primary users           |
| -- | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------- |
| 1  | Crowd intelligence     | People counts, density estimates, hotspot alerts, flow trends                 | Command centre          |
| 2  | Emergency SOS          | Medical, police, fire, rescue and general assistance requests                 | Pilgrims, responders    |
| 3  | Incident coordination  | Prioritization, duplicate reports, dispatch, escalation, closure              | Command centre          |
| 4  | Lost and found         | Missing-person cases, found-person cases, reunification workflow              | Pilgrims, help desks    |
| 5  | Multilingual assistant | Verified answers, voice input, event information, directions                  | Pilgrims                |
| 6  | GIS and navigation     | Ghats, roads, facilities, routes, closures and restricted areas               | All users               |
| 7  | Traffic and parking    | Parking occupancy, road closures, shuttle status and congestion               | Pilgrims, authorities   |
| 8  | Sanitation             | Toilet status, QR reports, cleaning assignments and verification              | Field teams             |
| 9  | Waste management       | Bin reports, collection tasks, overflow alerts and completion                 | Municipal teams         |
| 10 | River safety           | Official water-level alerts, safety zones and reported rescue incidents       | Authorities, pilgrims   |
| 11 | Command centre         | Unified map, alerts, cases, team status and operational reports               | Administrators          |
| 12 | Volunteer management   | Registration, roles, shifts, attendance and task allocation                   | Volunteers              |
| 13 | Medical services       | Hospitals, first aid, medical camps, ambulance requests                       | Pilgrims, medical teams |
| 14 | Public alerts          | Official announcements, weather alerts, route changes and evacuation notices  | Authorities, pilgrims   |
| 15 | Heritage and tourism   | Temple information, cultural programmes, audio guides and visitor information | Pilgrims                |

Important boundaries:

- Crowd analytics should estimate crowd levels, not identify individual pilgrims. Do not make facial recognition a default feature.
- AI-generated risk alerts are recommendations for trained human operators, not automatic declarations of danger.
- Missing-person records should be private by default. Public screens must not expose sensitive descriptions or photos.
- Water-quality and bathing-safety information should come from competent authorities. A prototype sensor reading must not be presented as proof that water is safe.
- Traffic diversions, evacuation instructions and other safety-critical public messages require authorized approval.

The global app research provides useful reference categories for these modules, but it does not establish that those external services offer usable APIs or integration rights.&#x20;

