### 4.2 Recommended technology stack

| Layer                             | Recommended choice                | Why                                            |
| --------------------------------- | --------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |
| Pilgrim, responder and field apps | React + TypeScript + Vite         | One reusable responsive frontend               |
| Admin dashboard                   | React + TypeScript                | Shared components and permissions              |
| UI styling                        | Tailwind CSS + shadcn/ui          | Fast, consistent interface development         |
| Maps                              | Leaflet + OpenStreetMap           | Flexible geospatial display                    |
| Backend                           | Python + FastAPI                  | Typed APIs and strong Python ecosystem         |
| Database                          | PostgreSQL + PostGIS              | Spatial queries and reliable relational data   |
| ORM and migrations                | SQLAlchemy + Alembic              | Maintainable schema evolution                  |
| Real-time                         | WebSockets                        | Live incidents and operational updates         |
| Cache and job queue               | Redis + Celery or equivalent      | Background processing and transient state      |
| Crowd AI                          | OpenCV + YOLO / P2PNet evaluation | Video processing and density estimation        |
| Offline support                   | PWA + IndexedDB                   | Local caching and queued operations            |
| Authentication                    | OIDC-compatible identity provider | Secure sign-in and role-based access           |
| Notifications                     | Web Push + FCM + SMS gateway      | Multi-channel communication                    |
| File storage                      | S3-compatible object storage      | Reports, authorized evidence and exports       |
| Monitoring                        | OpenTelemetry + structured logs   | Debugging, performance and auditability        |
| Deployment                        | Docker + managed database         | Reproducible deployment and simpler operations |

Solo-developer optimization: start with a single React codebase using separate route groups for each interface. Keep shared design components, but use distinct navigation and permissions for each role.

